Dunno.  I consider drinking totally un-idd potions to be quite
hazardous.

What could possibly go wrong?


1. Drink the potion of sickness. Lose points of strength which are
going to take awhile to get back.
2. Drink a potion of polymorph. Lose your armor.
3. Get confused, blind, or hallucinating.
4. Levitate and not be able to get down, starve to death in the air.

None of these *by themeselves* are lethal -- but in combination with
other things they can give you a very good chance to be killed.

I don't see that this adds much to the risk. Quaffing potions to find
out what they are without ANY precautions whatsoever is already pretty
hazardous.

And it's not all that hard to circumvent -- simply dip a waste dagger
or something in your un-ided potion before you taste it, and if you see
green stuff on the end, don't drink it.    An easy solution that costs
the user one turn to perform.

And if the player is in a habit of drinking potions without doing
*ANYTHING* to ID them prior -- well, this is only one of many ways to
dissuade them of the practice. 

